    "initial_reasoning": {
      "approach": "I would use a set to deduplicate the numbers in the list and then because sets have O(1) membership checks I can quickly check if certain numbers exist in the set. For example, to determine the start of the streak (n), I can check if n - 1 exist in the set. I can also check for n + 1 to determine if the streak continues. I will have two nested loops but since sets have O(1) membership checks, the overall time complexity would still be O(n) worst case. An important edge case would be a streak of 1, where n + 1 doesn't exist so the default placeholder variable would have to be at least 1",
